Display lines one after the other are one equations block (plan P3-29, D-S11): their rows align at `&`, each its own equation.

$ f(x) &= (x + 1)^2 $ <sq>
$ &= x^2 + 2 x + 1 $
$ &>= 2 x $ <bound>

A row break inside one formula keeps one number, on its last row:

$ g(x) &= sum_(k=0)^n binom(n, k) x^k \
  &= (1 + x)^n $ <binom>

Rows without `&` are centred each: $ a = 1 $ follows.

$ a + b = c $
$ d = e - f + g $

#{ const rows = [{src: 'u &= v + w', label: 'eq-u'}, 'v &= 2 w']; }
#math.equations(rows)

See @sq, @bound, @binom and @eq-u.
